   "id": 639740,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/9925f3015a5de872.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Subhadip Mondal/Biology Discussion)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The table shows which codons code for which amino acids in the DNA.</p>\n<p>Due to a mutation, the nucleotide sequence ATC-CAG-AGA becomes ATT-CAG-AGA on a gene.</p>\n<p>What type of mutation would this be?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1246491,
     "content_html": "Silent mutation."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246490,
     "content_html": "Missense mutation."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246489,
     "content_html": "Nonesense mutation."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246488,
     "content_html": "Frameshift mutation."
    }
   ],
